# Suppressions require a named stack pattern, a rationale, and a regression
# issue. The production C leak gate currently has no accepted leak suppression.

# Cross-GCC intentionally retains driver/cc1 allocation pools until process
# exit. These subprocesses only compile immutable guest fixtures; they never
# load or execute the production C engine.
leak:xmalloc
leak:xrealloc
leak:xcalloc
leak:operator new(unsigned long)

# GNU ld/BFD likewise keeps link graph and plugin pools until exit. This is the
# guest-fixture linker process, not the linked production engine.
leak:bfd_malloc
leak:bfd_zmalloc
leak:plugin_load_plugins
